# ==============================================================================
# x2gokdrive Configuration Template
# ==============================================================================
# This file configures default behavior for X2Go's KDrive server (x2gokdrive).
# It is sourced by the X2Go server to apply global defaults.
#
# NOTE: Many of these options can be overridden by the X2Go client session
# configuration. This file sets the baseline.
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# X2GO_X2GOKDRIVE_DEFAULT_OPTIONS
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Description:
#   Default options string passed to x2gokdrive.
#   These options are prepended/appended to the x2gokdrive command line.
#
# Syntax:
#   - Use standard x2gokdrive flags (e.g., "-geometry", "-depth").
#   - "-extension NAME" disables an extension.
#   - "+extension NAME" enables an extension.
#
# Reference:
#   Run `x2gokdrive -help` for the full list of supported options.
#
# Default:
#   Empty string.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
X2GO_X2GOKDRIVE_DEFAULT_OPTIONS="{{ X2GO_X2GOKDRIVE_DEFAULT_OPTIONS | default('\"\"') }}"

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GLX Extension Control (Commented Out by Default)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Description:
#   Disables the GLX extension. The old Mesa GLX implementation is often
#   outdated and can cause issues with modern desktop environments like GNOME 3
#   (e.g., unbreaking the control center).
#
# Warning:
#   Uncommenting this may improve stability for some desktop environments,
#   but will break OpenGL-based applications.
#
# Syntax:
#   X2GO_X2GOKDRIVE_DEFAULT_OPTIONS+=" -extension GLX"
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Uncomment the line below to disable GLX if you encounter display issues:
# X2GO_X2GOKDRIVE_DEFAULT_OPTIONS+=" -extension GLX"

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Network Listening Control
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Description:
#   Launches the X2Go agent (x2goagent) with the "-nolisten tcp" option.
#   This prevents the X server from listening on TCP ports, forcing X11
#   forwarding via Unix sockets (more secure and standard for X2Go).
#
# Recommendation:
#   This is the DEFAULT setting. X2Go developers STRONGLY RECOMMEND NOT
#   to change this unless you fully understand the security implications
#   and network configuration required for TCP-based X11.
#
# Syntax:
#   X2GO_X2GOKDRIVE_DEFAULT_OPTIONS+=" -nolisten tcp"
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
X2GO_X2GOKDRIVE_DEFAULT_OPTIONS+=" -nolisten tcp"

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Clipboard Behaviour
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Description:
#   Enforces global clipboard synchronization behaviour for all X2Go sessions.
#
# Possible Values:
#   - both  : Clipboard syncs both ways (Server <-> Client).
#   - server: Only Server to Client sync.
#   - client: Only Client to Server sync.
#   - none  : Clipboard sync is disabled.
#
# Default:
#   If commented out, individual clients can choose their own clipboard
#   behaviour in their X2Go client settings.
#
# Syntax:
#   X2GO_X2GOKDRIVE_DEFAULT_OPTIONS+=" -clipboard <value>"
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Uncomment to enforce a specific clipboard mode globally:
# X2GO_X2GOKDRIVE_DEFAULT_OPTIONS+=" -clipboard both"

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BIG-REQUESTS Extension Control
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Description:
#   Disables the BIG-REQUESTS X11 extension.
#
# Context:
#   Older versions of nx-libs did not implement BIG-REQUESTS correctly,
#   leading to crashes and instability. Newer versions handle it better,
#   but if you experience weird crashes related to large X11 requests,
#   uncommenting this line disables the extension to restore stability.
#
# Syntax:
#   X2GO_X2GOKDRIVE_DEFAULT_OPTIONS+=" -extension BIG-REQUESTS"
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Uncomment only if you experience crashes with large X11 operations:
# X2GO_X2GOKDRIVE_DEFAULT_OPTIONS+=" -extension BIG-REQUESTS"

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# X2GO_NXOPTIONS
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Description:
#   Extra nxagent options passed to the NX server component (x2goagent).
#   Options should be separated by commas.
#
# Example:
#   X2GO_NXOPTIONS="sleep=0,compression=high"
#
# Reference:
#   Consult nxagent documentation for supported options.
#
# Default:
#   Empty string.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
X2GO_NXOPTIONS="{{ X2GO_NXOPTIONS | default('\"\"') }}"